## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Project root resolution:** When the package is installed via `install_github`, the user's working directory may not be the repo root. The orchestration layer calls `system("Rscript modules/rna/...")` using relative paths. We need a strategy to resolve the project root. The proposed approach is:
> 1. Auto-detect by walking up from `getwd()` looking for the `modules/` directory
> 2. Allow explicit override via `set_omicsflow_root("path/to/OmicsFlow")`
> 3. Fall back to `getwd()` if detection fails
>
> **Does this approach work for your expected usage pattern?** (i.e., users will typically `setwd()` to the repo clone before running the pipeline)

> [!NOTE]
> **`modules/utils_metadata.R` dependency:** `validate_inputs()` currently `source()`s this file at runtime. In the packageized version, we'll resolve its path via `omicsflow_project_root()` rather than assuming it's relative to `getwd()`. The functions in `utils_metadata.R` are NOT moved into the package — they remain as shared scientific module utilities.

